1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,008
One marshmallow now, or two if you wait fifteen minutes. What would you pick?

2
00:00:06,458 --> 00:00:12,798
That choice has a name. Delayed gratification: skipping a small reward now for a bigger one later.

3
00:00:13,848 --> 00:00:19,673
In the famous marshmallow test, kids who could wait were linked to better results later in life.

4
00:00:20,923 --> 00:00:27,086
But your brain loves quick rewards. Scrolling, snacks, shopping. They feel good, then fade fast.

5
00:00:28,136 --> 00:00:32,564
The good news? Waiting is a skill. And like any skill, you can train it.

6
00:00:33,614 --> 00:00:37,540
Start small. Next time you want something, wait just ten minutes.

7
00:00:38,790 --> 00:00:41,906
So, one now or two later? Tell me in the comments.

8
00:00:43,556 --> 00:00:46,448
Follow me for more delayed gratification tips.

